autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "d5853ec3-6040-47cb-9bd6-1b54ca28441e", "created_at": "2026-09-17T05:31:45.161783", "failure_effects": ["M deklarerar sig offentligt som Tid\u00f6-blockets statsministerkandidat och publicerar en budgetmotion med profilvinster och en ansvarsfull finanspolitisk ram.", "M pekar offentligt p\u00e5 att S-V-C-MP-m\u00f6tet inte producerat ett bindande paket och att V:s tolerans inte \u00e4r s\u00e4krad.", "KD, L och/eller SD ansluter sig inte till motionen; Tid\u00f6-blocket framst\u00e5r som splittrat, KD:s block\u00f6verskridande reservsp\u00e5r f\u00f6rblir \u00f6ppet och M:s utspel uppfattas som f\u00f6rhastat, vilket f\u00f6rsvagar M:s initiativ."], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.6, "rationale": "Authority gate: M can bind itself (declare its own PM candidacy, publish its own budget motion, and make public statements grounded in authoritative effects 3945541d and c2d59786, which establish that the S-V-C-MP meeting failed to produce a binding package and that V's tolerance is not secured). M cannot unilaterally commit KD, L and SD to a joint motion; no prior commitment from those parties exists in the authoritative state, so the joint publication is an external consequence requiring their agreement. Prerequisite gate: no established commitments from KD/L/SD support the joint motion. Deterministic check: Tid\u00f6=173 cannot reach the 175 threshold without C, and S+C+V+MP=176 retains a majority, so the M-led path to the PM post remains blocked absent C's support; the 'path open for a future M-led solution' is therefore limited to keeping M's candidacy viable, not achieving a majority. Residual uncertainty concerns whether KD, L and SD actually join the joint motion, whether the bloc stays united, and whether KD's cross-bloc opening is toned down; given the parties' incentives (L's profile wins, SD's participation, KD's credible-alternative condition) this is moderately likely. The self-binding declaration and the factually grounded public statements occur in both branches.", "raw_output": {"failure_effects": ["M deklarerar sig offentligt som Tid\u00f6-blockets statsministerkandidat och publicerar en budgetmotion med profilvinster och en ansvarsfull finanspolitisk ram.", "M pekar offentligt p\u00e5 att S-V-C-MP-m\u00f6tet inte producerat ett bindande paket och att V:s tolerans inte \u00e4r s\u00e4krad.", "KD, L och/eller SD ansluter sig inte till motionen; Tid\u00f6-blocket framst\u00e5r som splittrat, KD:s block\u00f6verskridande reservsp\u00e5r f\u00f6rblir \u00f6ppet och M:s utspel uppfattas som f\u00f6rhastat, vilket f\u00f6rsvagar M:s initiativ."], "failure_supersedes_effect_ids": [], "mode": "probabilistic", "probability": 0.6, "rationale": "Authority gate: M can bind itself (declare its own PM candidacy, publish its own budget motion, and make public statements grounded in authoritative effects 3945541d and c2d59786, which establish that the S-V-C-MP meeting failed to produce a binding package and that V's tolerance is not secured). M cannot unilaterally commit KD, L and SD to a joint motion; no prior commitment from those parties exists in the authoritative state, so the joint publication is an external consequence requiring their agreement. Prerequisite gate: no established commitments from KD/L/SD support the joint motion. Deterministic check: Tid\u00f6=173 cannot reach the 175 threshold without C, and S+C+V+MP=176 retains a majority, so the M-led path to the PM post remains blocked absent C's support; the 'path open for a future M-led solution' is therefore limited to keeping M's candidacy viable, not achieving a majority. Residual uncertainty concerns whether KD, L and SD actually join the joint motion, whether the bloc stays united, and whether KD's cross-bloc opening is toned down; given the parties' incentives (L's profile wins, SD's participation, KD's credible-alternative condition) this is moderately likely. The self-binding declaration and the 